      "problem": "Consider the matrix\n  \n\n$$\nZ=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 1 & 4 & 9 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 8 & 3 & 7 & -2 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 3 & 8 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 6 & -3 & 0 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 8 & 5 & 3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 9 & 7 & 4 & 1 & 3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the dimensions of ${Z}^{T}?$\n\n${Z}^{T}$ is a \n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\times $\n{{field-2}}\n matrix.",
      "worked_solution": "When a matrix is transposed, its dimensions switch from $m\\times n$ to $n\\times m.$\n\nSo, since $Z$ is a $6\\times 7$ matrix, the transpose ${Z}^{T}$ is a $7\\times 6$ matrix.",
